# Plan: Prevent Duplicate Fragment Title for Cloned Cards in M@S Studio

## Summary
When a card is cloned in M@S Studio, the cloned fragment inherits the original title, which can create duplicates within the same tag path. This plan adds a uniqueness check that automatically appends a numeric suffix (`-1`, `-2`, …) to the cloned fragment's title before saving, scoped to the parent folder path. Manual title edits entered by the author in the clone dialog are not altered.

## Task Description
- Initialize the clone dialog title field with the source fragment's title (currently blank, so no-op saves go through unchanged).
- Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle, path)` to `mas-repository.js` that strips any existing `-N` suffix, searches existing fragment titles at the given path, and returns the lowest available `baseTitle-N` candidate.
- Call this helper inside `copyFragment` in `mas-repository.js` to resolve the final title before saving.
- Apply the same `titleClone` initialization fix to `editor-panel.js`, which contains a parallel clone flow.
- Add unit tests for `generateUniqueFragmentTitle`.

## Relevant Files

| File | Action | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `studio/src/mas-repository.js` | Edit | Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle`; use it in `copyFragment` |
| `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js` | Edit | Initialize `titleClone` to `this.fragment.title` in `showClone()` |
| `studio/src/editor-panel.js` | Edit | Same fix for parallel clone dialog in EditorPanel component |
| `studio/test/mas-repository.test.js` | Edit | Unit tests for `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` |

## Step by Step Tasks

### 1. Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` to `mas-repository.js`

Add a new async method to `MasRepository` (above `copyFragment`):

```js
async generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle, path) {
    // Strip existing numeric suffix: "card-2" -> "card"
    const suffixMatch = baseTitle.match(/^(.*)-(\d+)$/);
    const rootTitle = suffixMatch ? suffixMatch[1] : baseTitle;

    // Collect all fragment titles at the given path
    const existingTitles = new Set();
    try {
        const gen = this.aem.sites.cf.fragments.search({ path, query: rootTitle });
        for await (const items of gen) {
            for (const item of items) {
                existingTitles.add(item.title);
            }
        }
    } catch {
        return baseTitle; // Search failure: return original, do not block clone
    }

    if (!existingTitles.has(baseTitle)) return baseTitle;

    let n = 1;
    while (n <= 99) {
        const candidate = `${rootTitle}-${n}`;
        if (!existingTitles.has(candidate)) return candidate;
        n++;
    }
    return `${rootTitle}-${n}`;
}
```

### 2. Use the helper in `copyFragment` in `mas-repository.js`

Inside `copyFragment`, after the `copy(this.fragmentInEdit)` call resolves, derive the parent path from `result.path` and generate a unique title:

- Compute `const parentPath = result.path.split('/').slice(0, -1).join('/');`
- Compute `const requestedTitle = (updatedTitle && updatedTitle !== result.title) ? updatedTitle : result.title;`
- Await `const uniqueTitle = await this.generateUniqueFragmentTitle(requestedTitle, parentPath);`
- Replace the `needsSave` block so that if `uniqueTitle !== result.title || osi`, the title is set to `uniqueTitle` and a save is performed.

This ensures that even when the author leaves the title unchanged in the dialog, the cloned fragment gets a unique title.

### 3. Initialize `titleClone` in `showClone()` — `mas-fragment-editor.js`

In `MasFragmentEditor.showClone()`:
```js
async showClone() {
    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {
        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();
        if (!confirmed) return;
    }
    this.titleClone = this.fragment.title;  // <-- add this line
    this.showCloneDialog = true;
    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);
}
```

This ensures `titleClone` carries the current title when the dialog opens, so the correct value is passed to `copyFragment` when the author clicks "Clone" without typing.

### 4. Initialize `titleClone` in `showClone()` — `editor-panel.js`

Apply the identical one-line fix to `EditorPanel.showClone()` (line ~620) for the parallel clone flow used in the side-by-side editor panel:

```js
async showClone() {
    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {
        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();
        if (!confirmed) return;
    }
    this.titleClone = this.fragment.title;  // <-- add this line
    this.showCloneDialog = true;
    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);
}
```

### 5. Add unit tests in `mas-repository.test.js`

Add a new `describe('generateUniqueFragmentTitle')` block inside the existing test suite. Cover:

- Returns `baseTitle` unchanged when no fragments match at the path.
- Returns `baseTitle-1` when `baseTitle` already exists but `baseTitle-1` does not.
- Returns `baseTitle-2` when both `baseTitle` and `baseTitle-1` already exist.
- Strips an existing numeric suffix before incrementing: `baseTitle-1` → `baseTitle-2` (not `baseTitle-1-1`).
- Returns `baseTitle` (no throw) when the AEM search call rejects.

Test pattern (using existing sinon + esm-bundle/chai setup):
```js
describe('generateUniqueFragmentTitle', () => {
    it('returns the base title when no duplicate exists', async () => { … });
    it('appends -1 when base title already exists', async () => { … });
    it('increments to -2 when -1 already exists', async () => { … });
    it('strips existing suffix before incrementing', async () => { … });
    it('returns base title when search fails', async () => { … });
});
```

Use `sandbox.stub()` on `repository.aem.sites.cf.fragments.search` to return an async generator that yields mock title arrays.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Cloning a card with an existing Fragment Title generates a unique title with a `-N` suffix.
- The suffix increments correctly: `-1`, `-2`, `-3` for successive clones.
- Uniqueness is scoped to the parent folder path (same as the source fragment).
- The original card's Fragment Title is not modified.
- Authors can still type a custom title in the clone dialog; that value is deduplicated if needed but otherwise honored.
- No two cards share the same Fragment Title + folder path after a clone operation.

## Validation Commands
- `node --check studio/src/mas-repository.js`
- `node --check studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`
- `node --check studio/src/editor-panel.js`

